dports (2.4.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * update: replace the whiptail/dialog checklist with a full-screen
    checklist that shows the containers using each image, explains unknown
    statuses, scrolls, follows resizes and can select updates/all/none
  * update: report locally built images as "local"; only images with an
    update are selected by default (unknown and local ones no longer are)
  * update: add --check and --yes; report only when there is no terminal
  * update: print the docker compose command that recreates the containers
    of updated images
  * update: show progress, cap parallel registry queries at 8 and time each
    out after DPORTS_TIMEOUT seconds (default 30)
  * update: compare against the right arm variant on 32-bit ARM hosts
  * update: honour -C/--no-color and options given after "update"
  * fish: run "dports update" from dports.bash instead of a second copy
  * tunnel: fall back to the config file, instead of printing a bogus row,
    when cloudflared's metrics server returns no ingress rules
  * no separate "docker info" probe before every listing
  * installer: ask before removing the Debian package on uninstall (or use
    --apt / --no-apt); download the files of the matching release tag; do
    not use files from the current directory when piped to bash
  * packaging: require bash (>= 4.3), drop the whiptail recommendation
  * packaging: move Docker from Depends to Suggests (apt pulled in docker.io
    where Docker was installed from snap or static binaries); drop the empty
    postinst and prerm
  * packaging: set file modes explicitly so the build does not depend on
    the umask (it failed in CI containers running with umask 000)
  * tests: add tests/test_update.sh (make test) with a fake docker CLI

 -- JonPark0 <yeochoony@gmail.com>  Mon, 02 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000

dports (2.3.0) stable; urgency=medium

  * New -t/--tunnel option: list Cloudflare Tunnel hostnames and the
    containers they route to (from cloudflared's metrics server or config file)
  * update: detect updates correctly with the containerd image store (Docker
    Engine 29+ default), which reported every image as outdated
  * update: compare RepoDigests against the registry via buildx, with a
    manifest-inspect fallback; report "?" instead of guessing when unsure
  * update: resolve images through the container's configured reference, so
    containers still running an old image are no longer listed as bare IDs
  * update: skip digest-pinned images, detect pulls by image ID, and stop
    printing job-control notices when run as a shell function
  * update: remove eval of dialog output and traps that clobbered the
    calling shell's own traps
  * fish: run update checks in parallel (fish cannot background functions)
  * fish: ship completions separately so they work before the first run
  * -a/--all: show port bindings of stopped containers (docker ps omits them)
  * installer: fix raw escape codes in --help, report failed downloads in the
    dialog UI, only uninstall files that define dports, back up dotfiles
    before editing them, and honour --yes
  * packaging: move fish from Recommends to Suggests; recommend whiptail;
    accept docker-cli (Debian 13+) as the Docker CLI dependency

